.sp
Filter \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies object key name filtering rules. For information about key name filtering, see \fI\%Configuring event notifications using object key name filtering\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Key \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A container for object key name prefix and suffix filtering rules.
.sp
FilterRules \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A list of containers for the key\-value pair that defines the criteria for the filter rule.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the Amazon S3 object key name to filter on. An object key name is the name assigned to an object in your Amazon S3 bucket. You specify whether to filter on the suffix or prefix of the object key name. A prefix is a specific string of characters at the beginning of an object key name, which you can use to organize objects. For example, you can start the key names of related objects with a prefix, such as \fB2023\-\fP or \fBengineering/\fP . Then, you can use \fBFilterRule\fP to find objects in a bucket with key names that have the same prefix. A suffix is similar to a prefix, but it is at the end of the object key name instead of at the beginning.
.sp
Name \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The object key name prefix or suffix identifying one or more objects to which the filtering rule applies. The maximum length is 1,024 characters. Overlapping prefixes and suffixes are not supported. For more information, see \fI\%Configuring Event Notifications\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBprefix\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsuffix\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Value \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
